{#
  defra-internal — header

  The Defra top bar: the organisation lock-up on the left, and on the right the
  organisation the signed-in person works for.

  Two organisations, and the pair is the point. The lock-up is the department
  that owns the service; the name opposite it is the regulator using it. A
  person who works across regulators needs to see which one they are in before
  they read anything else on the page, so it sits in the identity bar rather
  than in the navigation below.

  It pairs with govuk-frontend's own service navigation, rendered next to this
  one rather than inside it — the same way the GOV.UK header and service
  navigation are two components combined on the page. The service name, the
  links, the signed-in person and Sign out all belong to that component, not to
  this one.

  params:
    organisationName  {string}  logo lock-up text; use <br> to control wrapping
    homepageUrl       {string}  where the lock-up links to (default "/")
    organisation      {string}  the organisation the signed-in person works
                                for, shown top right. Plain text, not a link —
                                it says where you are, it is not somewhere to
                                go. Omit it and nothing renders, which is what
                                a signed-out page and a documentation page
                                need.

  Styles: app/assets/sass/_defra-internal.scss
#}
{# No `role="banner"`. A top-level `<header>` already is one, and govuk-frontend
   dropped the explicit role from its own header for the same reason. #}
<header class="defra-internal-header">
  <div class="govuk-width-container">
    <div class="defra-internal-header__main">
      <div class="defra-internal-header__logo">
        <a class="defra-internal-header__logo-link" href="{{ params.homepageUrl | default('/') }}">
          {{ params.organisationName | default("Department for Environment,<br>Food &amp; Rural Affairs") | safe }}
        </a>
      </div>
      {% if params.organisation %}
        <p class="defra-internal-header__organisation">{{ params.organisation }}</p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
</header>
